{% set local_problem %}
<p>Trinity's established neighborhoods have mature tree coverage that keeps gutters filling year-round. Pine needles in particular are a constant problem — they slip through large-opening guards and accumulate in gutters throughout the year.</p>

<p>For many Trinity homeowners, gutter cleaning becomes a dreaded chore. Climbing ladders multiple times a year is inconvenient and risky. Professional cleaning costs $150-200 per visit — money that adds up fast.</p>

<p>The bigger concern is what happens between cleanings. When gutters clog during Morgan County's heavy storms, water overflows toward your foundation. On clay soil, that overflow pools and persists, creating conditions for foundation damage.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve this permanently. Install once, and the cleaning burden is essentially eliminated. As your closest gutter company, we'll help you choose the right system.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers that fit over or inside your gutters, allowing water through while blocking debris. Different types work better for different challenges.</p>

<p>Micro-mesh guards with tiny perforations excel at blocking fine debris like pine needles. Screen guards handle larger leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water into the gutter while debris slides off.</p>

<p>For Trinity homes, we typically recommend micro-mesh guards. They handle both fine and coarse debris, work well with the area's tree mix, and withstand heavy debris loads during storms.</p>
{% endset %}

